Funding-Text = {We are indebted to Philippe Bouchet at the MNHN for friendship and
   continued access to collections over many years, which have been
   fundamental for our phylogenetic analyses. Grateful thanks are due to
   the Paris team of Philippe Maestrati, Virginie Heros and, in particular,
   Barbara Buge, curator of the molecular samples. For arranging loans and
   sampling of rare lucinids, we thank Bruce Marshall (Museum of New
   Zealand TePapa Tongarewa, Wellington, New Zealand), Manuel Malaquias
   (University of Bergen Museum, Bergen, Norway) and Gustav Paulay (Florida
   Museum of Natural History, University of Florida, USA). For assistance
   with sequencing at NHMUK, we thank Chiho Ikebe, Claire Griffin, Lisa
   Smith and Vassia Koutsouvel. We thank Laetitia Wilkins for her
   contribution of rare specimens from both sides of the Isthmus of Panama,
   Jay Osvatic for his technical contributions to the bioinformatic
   processing of lucinid metagenome reads and Jill Petersen for sharing the
   metagenome data. NGS sequencing was carried out at the DNA Technologies
